nce? Many people who do this report: - More stable energy throughout the day - Better sleep quality - Improved mood and mental clarity - Faster recovery from exercise - Fewer aches and pains - Clearer skin and better digestion They didn't realize they were running below their potential until they experienced a higher baseline. So yes, some people survive on junk food. But the science suggests that *almost everyone* would be healthier, feel better, and age more slowly on a better diet. The exceptions you've seen are real, but they are not evidence that diet doesn't matter—they are evidence that human resilience is remarkable, and that we often don't know what we're missing.
